e leading zeros unless stored as text.\n- Embedded commas/newlines/quotes: these affect CSV parsing; either remove them or ensure proper quoting/escape rules and verify portal behavior.\n- Encoding and delimiters: confirm the portal expects UTF‑8 and the delimiter (comma, semicolon, tab).\n- Merged cells, conditional formatting, and comments/notes: these won’t transfer — extract any needed info into plain cells first.\n- Row limits and column headers: verify portal limits and required header row or column order.\n- Audit totals: after converting to CSV, reconfirm sum totals and counts match the original.\n\nSafe sequence to prepare (concise)\n1. Make a quick backup copy of the workbook.\n2. Create a working copy of the budget tab (duplicate the sheet or new workbook).\n3. Resolve references: bring the referenced sheet(s) data into the working copy or paste the referenced ranges as values where SUMIFs point to, so the working sheet is self-contained.\n4. Replace formulas with values: select all → Copy → Paste Special → Values (this preserves the calculated numbers).\n5. Fix formatting-sensitive items: force text for IDs with leading zeros, standardize date format, remove or escape commas/newlines if needed.\n6. Check for errors/circular refs and fix them.\n7. Save/export the working copy as CSV (or copy/paste values into the portal) using UTF‑8 and the correct delimiter.\n8. Open the CSV in a plain text editor to verify layout, encoding, delimiter, headers, and totals.\n9. Upload/paste to the portal and spot-check key totals and a few random rows against the original.\n\nIf you want, paste the sheet here (or tell me which columns reference the other sheet) and I can point out the exact SUMIFs and references you need to flatten or bring into the CSV.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_02e752598c3ad88c016a9a0981bc3c87d09fe76d0c7fa7b2c8","role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0.0,"previous_response_id":nul